{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-21\nattempt=1\nbase=c679e58d418e2151ad037b06057ebf097d26cc87\ncandidate=628888f2468a11570f68c14732c72e1d8893260d\n\nDESIGN:\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-21 delivers the Huddle browser shell: every HTTP node serves a same-origin SPA at `GET /`, and that SPA owns sign-up/login UI, visible validation errors, auto-login after success, session restore via `localStorage` key `huddle.token`, and logout that returns the user to the auth modal. It consumes the already-landed MARATHON-3 contracts (`POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`) without adding auth APIs, and leaves a documented authenticated-shell mount point for MARATHON-22 (workspaces/channels/messages) and MARATHON-23 (threads/settings). Pinned DOM hooks (`data-testid` / `id`) make the auth flow automatable at **1280×900**.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n1. **Static SPA assets under `/app/public/`**, served by each Node worker with stdlib `fs` + `http` (no Express, no bundler, no npm frontend deps). Entry document is `public/index.html`; client logic in `public/js/auth.js` + `public/js/app.js`; styles in `public/css/app.css`. Scripts load as classic or deferred `<script src=\"…\">` (no build step in `start.sh`).\n2. **Same-origin `fetch`** to `/api/auth/*` with `Content-Type: application/json`. Token persistence **only** at `localStorage['huddle.token']` (exact key per MARATHON-3). Authenticated calls send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.\n3. **Client-owned logout:** clear `huddle.token`, clear in-memory session/user, show `#auth-modal`. No `POST /api/auth/logout` (explicitly out of MARATHON-3; server tokens may remain until a future revoke task).\n4. **Two UI phases in this task only:**\n   - **Unauthenticated:** `#auth-modal` visible with sign-up **or** login form (toggled by `auth-toggle`).\n   - **Authenticated shell:** modal hidden; chrome shows `current-user` + `logout-btn`; a `#app-shell` placeholder hosts future MARATHON-22 content (empty or minimal “signed in” copy is fine; **must not** invent workspace/channel APIs here).\n5. **Boot sequence:** on `DOMContentLoaded`, if `huddle.token` is set → `GET /api/auth/me` → success enters shell with returned `user`; `401`/network failure clears token and shows auth modal. Register/login success writes token then enters shell using the response `user` (auto-login; optional immediate `/me` is allowed but not required).\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| React/Vite/Webpack SPA | Needs install + build; epic requires self-contained `/app` with no remote services; MARATHON-2/3 used zero npm deps |\n| Server-rendered login forms | Task asks for SPA shell and client `localStorage`; SSR would fight MARATHON-22 client routing |\n| Cookie/`HttpOnly` sessions | MARATHON-3 fixed opaque Bearer + `huddle.token`; changing storage breaks the declared SPA/WS/IRC token story |\n| Serve SPA only from node 0 | Task: “on any node”; QA may hit `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` interchangeably |\n| Implement workspace restore UI here | Belongs to MARATHON-22; this task only restores **auth session** and clears shell state so 22 can reload domain data after re-login |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nA vanilla multi-file SPA is less ergonomic than a framework, but keeps the cluster zero-dependency and matches the existing Node stdlib style. Client-only logout leaves orphaned token rows in SQLite; acceptable until an explicit revoke endpoint is tasked.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | App root `/app`; HTTP `server/index.js`; ports `8000+NODE_ID`; API under `/api/...`; JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`; browser UI at **`GET /`** (disk path `/app` ≠ URL path) |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven string fields; register/login/me envelopes; errors `{ \"error\": string }`; username `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$`; password length ≥ 8; `huddle.token`; Bearer header; no email required |\n| MARATHON-4 (design only) | Future profile PATCH; on `401` clear `huddle.token` and show login — same logout path this shell owns |\n\n### Conventions fixed here (for\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=628888f2468a11570f68c14732c72e1d8893260d APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=628888f2468a11570f68c14732c72e1d8893260d CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"8c969c8e-77c9-4261-a386-a66451852833"}
