{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-4f7f68fb-377f-46bf-ba96-2649525f7485-18\nfc_e42ee057-0fe4-9981-9411-fea635b204e3_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"command -v loom; loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 50000; ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/ 2>/dev/null | head","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-4f7f68fb-377f-46bf-ba96-2649525f7485-18\nfc_e42ee057-0fe4-9981-9411-fea635b204e3_0","simpleCommands":["command","loom","head","ls","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"command","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-v"},{"type":"word","value":"loom"}],"fullText":"command -v loom"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"50000"}],"fullText":"head -c 50000"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/"}],"fullText":"ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/"},{"name":"head","args":[],"fullText":"head"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch MARATHON-21 task design via loom","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8c969c8e-77c9-4261-a386-a66451852833","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"command -v loom; loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 50000; ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/ 2>/dev/null | head","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-21 delivers the Huddle browser shell: every HTTP node serves a same-origin SPA at `GET /`, and that SPA owns sign-up/login UI, visible validation errors, auto-login after success, session restore via `localStorage` key `huddle.token`, and logout that returns the user to the auth modal. It consumes the already-landed MARATHON-3 contracts (`POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`) without adding auth APIs, and leaves a documented authenticated-shell mount point for MARATHON-22 (workspaces/channels/messages) and MARATHON-23 (threads/settings). Pinned DOM hooks (`data-testid` / `id`) make the auth flow automatable at **1280×900**.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n1. **Static SPA assets under `/app/public/`**, served by each Node worker with stdlib `fs` + `http` (no Express, no bundler, no npm frontend deps). Entry document is `public/index.html`; client logic in `public/js/auth.js` + `public/js/app.js`; styles in `public/css/app.css`. Scripts load as classic or deferred `\\u003cscript src=\\\"…\\\"\\u003e` (no build step in `start.sh`).\\n2. **Same-origin `fetch`** to `/api/auth/*` with `Content-Type: application/json`. Token persistence **only** at `localStorage['huddle.token']` (exact key per MARATHON-3). Authenticated calls send `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e`.\\n3. **Client-owned logout:** clear `huddle.token`, clear in-memory session/user, show `#auth-modal`. No `POST /api/auth/logout` (explicitly out of MARATHON-3; server tokens may remain until a future revoke task).\\n4. **Two UI phases in this task only:**\\n   - **Unauthenticated:** `#auth-modal` visible with sign-up **or** login form (toggled by `auth-toggle`).\\n   - **Authenticated shell:** modal hidden; chrome shows `current-user` + `logout-btn`; a `#app-shell` placeholder hosts future MARATHON-22 content (empty or minimal “signed in” copy is fine; **must not** invent workspace/channel APIs here).\\n5. **Boot sequence:** on `DOMContentLoaded`, if `huddle.token` is set → `GET /api/auth/me` → success enters shell with returned `user`; `401`/network failure clears token and shows auth modal. Register/login success writes token then enters shell using the response `user` (auto-login; optional immediate `/me` is allowed but not required).\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\\n|-------------|--------------|\\n| React/Vite/Webpack SPA | Needs install + build; epic requires self-contained `/app` with no remote services; MARATHON-2/3 used zero npm deps |\\n| Server-rendered login forms | Task asks for SPA shell and client `localStorage`; SSR would fight MARATHON-22 client routing |\\n| Cookie/`HttpOnly` sessions | MARATHON-3 fixed opaque Bearer + `huddle.token`; changing storage breaks the declared SPA/WS/IRC token story |\\n| Serve SPA only from node 0 | Task: “on any node”; QA may hit `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` interchangeably |\\n| Implement workspace restore UI here | Belongs to MARATHON-22; this task only restores **auth session** and clears shell state so 22 can reload domain data after re-login |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\nA vanilla multi-file SPA is less ergonomic than a framework, but keeps the cluster zero-dependency and matches the existing Node stdlib style. Client-only logout leaves orphaned token rows in SQLite; acceptable until an explicit revoke endpoint is tasked.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\\n| Source | Convention |\\n|--------|------------|\\n| MARATHON-2 | App root `/app`; HTTP `server/index.js`; ports `8000+NODE_ID`; API under `/api/...`; JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`; browser UI at **`GET /`** (disk path `/app` ≠ URL path) |\\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven string fields; register/login/me envelopes; errors `{ \\\"error\\\": string }`; username `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$`; password length ≥ 8; `huddle.token`; Bearer header; no email required |\\n| MARATHON-4 (design only) | Future profile PATCH; on `401` clear `huddle.token` and show login — same logout path this shell owns |\\n\\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| Static root | `/app/public/` (repo path `public/`) |\\n| Token storage key | `localStorage` key **`huddle.token`** exactly (string token only; do not store full `UserObj` as the session source of truth) |\\n| Auth modal | Element **`id=\\\"auth-modal\\\"`** |\\n| Pinned testids | `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`, `current-user`, `logout-btn` |\\n| Auth mode toggle | `auth-toggle` switches register ↔ login **without** navigation |\\n| Display identity | `current-user` text content = `user.display_name` (fallback `user.username` if empty) |\\n| Shell mount | `#app-shell` (or equivalent stable id) — MARATHON-22 attaches three-pane UI here; must exist when authenticated |\\n| Viewport | Primary layout usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scroll for auth chrome |\\n| Asset URLs | Absolute-from-root paths `/css/...`, `/js/...` so any node origin works |\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### C-SPA-1 — `GET /` (and static assets) — **Backend owns serve; Frontend owns behavior**\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Method / path | `GET /` |\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Success | `200`, `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8`, body = SPA document that loads CSS/JS |\\n| Other methods on `/` | `405` `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"method_not_allowed\\\" }` **or** `404` JSON; must not `500` |\\n\\n**Also serve (same task):**\\n| Path | Type | Notes |\\n|------|------|-------|\\n| `GET /css/app.css` | `text/css; charset=utf-8` | From `public/css/app.css` |\\n| `GET /js/app.js`, `GET /js/auth.js` (and any other files under `public/js/`) | `application/javascript; charset=utf-8` | Path traversal forbidden |\\n| `GET /` only as HTML entry | — | Do **not** require `/index.html` for acceptance; optional redirect/`index.html` alias is allowed |\\n\\n**Routing order in `server/index.js` (must preserve API contracts):**\\n1. `GET /api/health` (unchanged)\\n2. Auth API via `handleAuthRoutes` (unchanged)\\n3. Static / SPA handler for safe paths under `public/`\\n4. Else `404` `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"not_found\\\" }`\\n\\n**Path safety:** resolve files under `path.join(__dirname, '..', 'public')` (or `/app/public`); reject `..` segments; never serve outside `public/`. Missing file → `404` JSON (same envelope as today) or plain 404 — not `500`.\\n\\n**Client while slow:** N/A for document fetch beyond browser load; if CSS/JS 404, auth UI may be unstyled but HTML structure with testids must still be present in the HTML (prefer embedding critical hooks in `index.html`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-2 — Client → `POST /api/auth/register` (consume MARATHON-3 C1)\\n\\n| Client sends | `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string, \\\"display_name\\\"?: string }` |\\n| Success | `201` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Errors | `400` / `409` / `5xx` with `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` when provided |\\n\\n**Client ownership:**\\n- Serialize JSON; **MUST NOT** require or gate on `email`.\\n- On submit: disable `auth-submit` (or equivalent pending state) until response settles.\\n- On `201`: `localStorage.setItem('huddle.token', token)`; set current user from `user`; hide `#auth-modal`; show authenticated chrome (**auto-login**).\\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string **visibly** inside the auth form (dedicated error element adjacent to the form; must be readable without opening DevTools).\\n- On network failure / `5xx`: show a visible generic message (e.g. “Something went wrong”); do not clear an existing valid token unless this was not a logged-in flow.\\n- Optional client pre-check (username regex / password length) may run before fetch; **server remains authoritative** — still handle server errors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-3 — Client → `POST /api/auth/login` (consume MARATHON-3 C2)\\n\\nSame as register for storage and error visibility; success status is `200`. Wrong password / unknown user → `401` → visible error; **MUST NOT** enter authenticated shell.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-4 — Client → `GET /api/auth/me` (consume MARATHON-3 C3)\\n\\n| When | App boot if `huddle.token` present; optionally after login |\\n| Header | `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Success `200` | Enter shell with `user`; keep token |\\n| `401` | `localStorage.removeItem('huddle.token')`; show `#auth-modal`; clear `current-user` |\\n| Network / `5xx` while booting with a token | Show auth modal **or** a non-claiming loading state, then fall back to auth modal; **MUST NOT** leave a forged `current-user` without a successful `/me` or prior successful register/login in this page life. Prefer: treat boot failure like logged-out after clear-or-keep policy — **decision: on boot network/`5xx`, keep token in storage but show a visible retry/error in the modal region and do not mark user logged-in; user can retry or clear via attempting login. On `401`, always clear token.** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-5 — Logout / re-login (client-only)\\n\\n| Action | Behavior |\\n|--------|----------|\\n| Click `logout-btn` | Remove `huddle.token`; clear in-memory `user` and any shell selection state this task owns; hide authenticated chrome; show `#auth-modal` in **login** mode; clear password fields |\\n| Login again (same or other user) | On `200`, store new token, show shell with new `user` |\\n| “Restores workspace” meaning for **this** task | Re-entering the authenticated shell after logout→login (and after hard reload with valid token). **Domain** workspace/channel/message tree reload is **MARATHON-22**: this task exposes a stable “session became authenticated” / “session cleared” seam (e.g. `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('huddle:auth', { detail: { user } }))` and `huddle:logout`) so 22 can refetch. Until 22 lands, shell may be empty — that is success for 21 |\\n\\n**MUST NOT:** call a non-existent logout API; leave `huddle.token` set after logout; show `current-user` while modal is the active unauthenticated UI.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-6 — DOM contract (QA / Playwright)\\n\\nExact attributes (implementer must not rename):\\n\\n| Hook | Requirement |\\n|------|-------------|\\n| `#auth-modal` | Present in DOM; visible when logged out; not the primary interactive surface when logged in (hidden via CSS `display:none` / `hidden` attribute / equivalent) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"]` | The sign-up/login `\\u003cform\\u003e` inside the modal |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-submit\\\"]` | Submit control (button or input) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-toggle\\\"]` | Control that switches between Sign up and Log in modes |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"current-user\\\"]` | Visible when authenticated; text identifies the user (`display_name`) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"logout-btn\\\"]` | Visible when authenticated; triggers C-SPA-5 |\\n\\nForm fields (recommended stable hooks for typing; if not testid-pinned by task, use `name` attributes):\\n- `name=\\\"username\\\"`, `name=\\\"password\\\"`\\n- Optional `name=\\\"display_name\\\"` visible **only** in sign-up mode\\n\\nError surface: an element inside `#auth-modal` / `auth-form` that displays the latest error string (e.g. `data-testid=\\\"auth-error\\\"` is **recommended** for clarity but **not** required by the task text — if omitted, error text must still be visible in the modal).\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Server schema\\n**No SQLite / API schema changes.** Reuses MARATHON-3 `users` / `tokens` and `UserObj`.\\n\\n### Browser persistence\\n| Key | Type | Nullability | Notes |\\n|-----|------|-------------|-------|\\n| `localStorage['huddle.token']` | string | absent when logged out | Opaque bearer ≥16 chars from API; never store password |\\n| In-memory `currentUser` | `UserObj` \\\\| null | null when logged out | Rebuilt from register/login/`/me`; not the durability source |\\n\\n### Backward compatibility\\nAdding `GET /` HTML where unknown paths previously returned JSON `404` is an intentional behavior change for `/` and static paths only. All `/api/*` contracts remain unchanged.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `public/index.html` | SPA shell: `#auth-modal`, form with pinned testids, `#app-shell`, links to CSS/JS |\\n| `public/css/app.css` | Layout for auth modal + minimal authenticated chrome; usable at 1280×900 |\\n| `public/js/auth.js` | Token get/set/clear; `register` / `login` / `me` fetch helpers; Bearer header helper |\\n| `public/js/app.js` | Boot, mode toggle, submit handlers, logout, show/hide modal vs shell, populate `current-user` |\\n| `server/static.js` | `handleStatic(req, res, pathname) → boolean`: map `/` → `index.html`, safe file serve under `public/`, correct Content-Types |\\n\\n### Modify\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/index.js` | After health + auth routes, call `handleStatic`; only then JSON 404. Do not alter health/auth status codes |\\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Optional: add `sendText(res, status, body, contentType)` used by static handler — keep `sendJson`/`readJson` behavior identical |\\n| `test/server.test.js` (optional but recommended) | Assert `GET /` returns `200` and `text/html` containing `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`; assert `/api/health` still JSON |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/db.js` | Auth API owned by MARATHON-3; no logout endpoint in this task |\\n| `start.sh`, `redis.conf` | Cluster bootstrap unchanged; static files need no extra process |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\\n| Workspace/channel/message UI | MARATHON-22 / 23 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Within this task\\n1. `public/index.html` + CSS skeleton with pinned hooks  \\n2. `server/static.js` + wire `index.js` so `GET /` works on any node  \\n3. `auth.js` API helpers  \\n4. `app.js` boot / submit / logout flows  \\n5. Manual check: register → token in localStorage → reload → still logged in → logout → login  \\n\\n### Parallelism\\n- Frontend implementer owns `public/**` + static routing.\\n- Backend auth already closed (MARATHON-3); do not block on MARATHON-4/5.\\n- MARATHON-22 **architecture/implementation** depends on: authenticated shell mount, `huddle.token`, `huddle:auth` / `huddle:logout` events (or equivalent documented callbacks), and existing testids remaining stable.\\n\\n### Seams this task owns\\n| Seam | Downstream |\\n|------|------------|\\n| `GET /` HTML + static assets | QA; all SPA tasks |\\n| `huddle.token` read/write/clear | MARATHON-22/23 fetch; MARATHON-18 WS `?token=` can read same key |\\n| DOM testids / `#auth-modal` | QA automation |\\n| Auth session events / `#app-shell` | MARATHON-22 three-pane; MARATHON-23 modals |\\n\\n### Build order\\n- **Requires:** MARATHON-3 endpoints on the integrated head (present).\\n- **Blocks:** Meaningful MARATHON-22 UI (declared dependent).\\n- **Does not block:** MARATHON-4/5 backend work.\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\\n| Cut | Owner |\\n|-----|--------|\\n| Workspaces, channels, three-pane, messages, their testids | MARATHON-22 |\\n| Threads, reactions, settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\\n| Profile PATCH UI | MARATHON-23 (API MARATHON-4) |\\n| Server token revoke / logout API | New task if ever required |\\n| Client-side router for deep links beyond `/` | MARATHON-22 if needed |\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\nNeighborhood scan (`server/`, `server/auth/`, `test/`, repo greps for `localStorage`, `auth-form`, `SPA`, `static`, `index.html`):\\n\\n| Finding | Why excluded |\\n|---------|----------------|\\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me | Already implemented (MARATHON-3); consume only |\\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` / tokens / users / passwords | No change |\\n| `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\\n| `test/auth.test.js` API contract tests | Remain backend-focused; optional SPA smoke is this task only if added under Files to Modify |\\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Workspaces / channels / messages UI + testids | MARATHON-22 |\\n| Threads / reactions / settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\\n| WS subscribe / `?token=` | MARATHON-18 |\\n| IRC gateway | MARATHON-20 |\\n| Server-side logout / token TTL | Explicitly deferred in MARATHON-3 |\\n| Email, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / unspecified |\\n\\nNo existing `public/` tree or `huddle.token` client code was found — greenfield SPA.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Empty username/password submit | Client may block with visible validation **or** send and show server `400`; either way user sees an error; no silent no-op |\\n| Password length \\u0026lt; 8 on register | Visible error (client and/or server `400`) |\\n| Duplicate username | Show server `409` `error` text in form |\\n| Invalid credentials on login | Show error; stay on modal; token unset |\\n| Double-click submit | Ignore second submit while request in flight (disable button) |\\n| `localStorage` unavailable / throws | Show visible error that auth cannot persist; do not pretend success |\\n| Stale token on boot (`401` from `/me`) | Clear `huddle.token`; show modal; no shell |\\n| Boot with token, network down | Do not show a fake user; show modal or retry UI; keep token until `401` or explicit logout |\\n| Logout | Token removed synchronously before UI switches; `current-user` cleared |\\n| Login as user B after user A | Shell shows B’s `display_name`; no leftover A identity in chrome |\\n| Hard reload while logged in | Token survives; `/me` restores shell |\\n| `GET /` on `:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002` | Identical SPA (any node) |\\n| Request `GET /../../etc/passwd` style path | Rejected; `404`; no file leak |\\n| `POST /` | Not an API; `405` or `404`; not `500` |\\n| Auth API still JSON | Static handler must not intercept `/api/*` |\\n| Toggle sign-up ↔ login | Clears or retains username per UX choice; **must** clear visible error; password field cleared on toggle **recommended** |\\n| Viewport 1280×900 | Auth modal and chrome fully usable; no reliance on hover-only controls for submit/logout/toggle |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and `:8001`, `:8002`) returns **200** HTML for the SPA (not JSON `not_found`).\\n2. HTML includes `#auth-modal` and elements with `data-testid` values **`auth-form`**, **`auth-submit`**, **`auth-toggle`**, **`current-user`**, **`logout-btn`**.\\n3. From a logged-out state, user can **sign up** with valid username/password; on success they are **immediately authenticated** (modal dismissed; `current-user` shows identity) without a separate manual login step.\\n4. After sign-up/login success, `localStorage.getItem('huddle.token')` is a non-empty string (length ≥ 16).\\n5. Invalid register (short password, bad username) shows a **visible** error in the auth UI; user remains logged out; token **MUST NOT** be set.\\n6. Login with wrong password shows a **visible** error; token **MUST NOT** be set; shell **MUST NOT** appear.\\n7. `auth-toggle` switches the form between sign-up and login modes without full page navigation.\\n8. Clicking `logout-btn` clears `huddle.token`, hides authenticated chrome, and shows `#auth-modal` again.\\n9. After logout, logging in again returns the user to the authenticated shell (session restored for SPA purposes).\\n10. Hard reload with a valid token still logged-in (via `/api/auth/me`); hard reload after logout stays logged-out.\\n11. Layout is operable at **1280×900**.\\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or `/api/auth/*` response shapes/status codes.\\n13. **MUST NOT** require `email` in the form as a mandatory field.\\n14. **MUST NOT** introduce remote CDNs, Slack SDK, or a frontend build that `start.sh` must run.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (implementer)\\n- Unit/integration: `GET /` → 200 + `text/html` + substring `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`.\\n- Existing `test/auth.test.js` still passes (API unchanged).\\n- Optional: static path traversal attempt returns 404.\\n\\n### Manual / browser (human or QA)\\n1. Start cluster (`./start.sh`); open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\\n2. Sign up `alice` / `password1` → see `current-user`, DevTools Application → `huddle.token` set.\\n3. Reload → still logged in.\\n4. Logout → token gone, modal visible.\\n5. Login → shell returns.\\n6. Toggle to sign-up, try password `short` → visible error.\\n7. Repeat smoke on `:8001` (register on 8000, open 8001 with same origin storage is per-port — use login on 8001 with same credentials to prove API; note **localStorage is origin-scoped per port**, so cross-port auto-session is **not** required; cross-node token validity remains a backend property).\\n\\n### Explicit non-goals for verification\\nWorkspace lists, messages, threads, WS — verify only auth shell + token lifecycle here.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"SPA shell served from GET / on any node via public/ + server/static.js. Auth uses huddle.token, pinned testids, client-only logout, huddle:auth/huddle:logout events + #app-shell for MARATHON-22. Verified unit tests + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/logout/reload/validation).\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.142443715Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:58:35.262638318Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up/login form with visible validation errors; auto-login on success; logout/login restores workspace. Store token in localStorage huddle.token. Pin data-testid: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, current-user, logout-btn; ids auth-modal. Drivable at 1280x900.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-22\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: workspaces, channels, three-pane layout, messages\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.163337652Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 25,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"author\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=628888f2468a11570f68c14732c72e1d8893260d\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:58:35.238705649Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nloom-prompts\npackage.json\nredis.conf\nserver\nstart.sh\ntest\ntimer.sh\n","stderr":"","executionTime":96,"interleavedOutput":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-21 delivers the Huddle browser shell: every HTTP node serves a same-origin SPA at `GET /`, and that SPA owns sign-up/login UI, visible validation errors, auto-login after success, session restore via `localStorage` key `huddle.token`, and logout that returns the user to the auth modal. It consumes the already-landed MARATHON-3 contracts (`POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`) without adding auth APIs, and leaves a documented authenticated-shell mount point for MARATHON-22 (workspaces/channels/messages) and MARATHON-23 (threads/settings). Pinned DOM hooks (`data-testid` / `id`) make the auth flow automatable at **1280×900**.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n1. **Static SPA assets under `/app/public/`**, served by each Node worker with stdlib `fs` + `http` (no Express, no bundler, no npm frontend deps). Entry document is `public/index.html`; client logic in `public/js/auth.js` + `public/js/app.js`; styles in `public/css/app.css`. Scripts load as classic or deferred `\\u003cscript src=\\\"…\\\"\\u003e` (no build step in `start.sh`).\\n2. **Same-origin `fetch`** to `/api/auth/*` with `Content-Type: application/json`. Token persistence **only** at `localStorage['huddle.token']` (exact key per MARATHON-3). Authenticated calls send `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e`.\\n3. **Client-owned logout:** clear `huddle.token`, clear in-memory session/user, show `#auth-modal`. No `POST /api/auth/logout` (explicitly out of MARATHON-3; server tokens may remain until a future revoke task).\\n4. **Two UI phases in this task only:**\\n   - **Unauthenticated:** `#auth-modal` visible with sign-up **or** login form (toggled by `auth-toggle`).\\n   - **Authenticated shell:** modal hidden; chrome shows `current-user` + `logout-btn`; a `#app-shell` placeholder hosts future MARATHON-22 content (empty or minimal “signed in” copy is fine; **must not** invent workspace/channel APIs here).\\n5. **Boot sequence:** on `DOMContentLoaded`, if `huddle.token` is set → `GET /api/auth/me` → success enters shell with returned `user`; `401`/network failure clears token and shows auth modal. Register/login success writes token then enters shell using the response `user` (auto-login; optional immediate `/me` is allowed but not required).\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\\n|-------------|--------------|\\n| React/Vite/Webpack SPA | Needs install + build; epic requires self-contained `/app` with no remote services; MARATHON-2/3 used zero npm deps |\\n| Server-rendered login forms | Task asks for SPA shell and client `localStorage`; SSR would fight MARATHON-22 client routing |\\n| Cookie/`HttpOnly` sessions | MARATHON-3 fixed opaque Bearer + `huddle.token`; changing storage breaks the declared SPA/WS/IRC token story |\\n| Serve SPA only from node 0 | Task: “on any node”; QA may hit `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` interchangeably |\\n| Implement workspace restore UI here | Belongs to MARATHON-22; this task only restores **auth session** and clears shell state so 22 can reload domain data after re-login |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\nA vanilla multi-file SPA is less ergonomic than a framework, but keeps the cluster zero-dependency and matches the existing Node stdlib style. Client-only logout leaves orphaned token rows in SQLite; acceptable until an explicit revoke endpoint is tasked.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\\n| Source | Convention |\\n|--------|------------|\\n| MARATHON-2 | App root `/app`; HTTP `server/index.js`; ports `8000+NODE_ID`; API under `/api/...`; JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`; browser UI at **`GET /`** (disk path `/app` ≠ URL path) |\\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven string fields; register/login/me envelopes; errors `{ \\\"error\\\": string }`; username `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$`; password length ≥ 8; `huddle.token`; Bearer header; no email required |\\n| MARATHON-4 (design only) | Future profile PATCH; on `401` clear `huddle.token` and show login — same logout path this shell owns |\\n\\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| Static root | `/app/public/` (repo path `public/`) |\\n| Token storage key | `localStorage` key **`huddle.token`** exactly (string token only; do not store full `UserObj` as the session source of truth) |\\n| Auth modal | Element **`id=\\\"auth-modal\\\"`** |\\n| Pinned testids | `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`, `current-user`, `logout-btn` |\\n| Auth mode toggle | `auth-toggle` switches register ↔ login **without** navigation |\\n| Display identity | `current-user` text content = `user.display_name` (fallback `user.username` if empty) |\\n| Shell mount | `#app-shell` (or equivalent stable id) — MARATHON-22 attaches three-pane UI here; must exist when authenticated |\\n| Viewport | Primary layout usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scroll for auth chrome |\\n| Asset URLs | Absolute-from-root paths `/css/...`, `/js/...` so any node origin works |\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### C-SPA-1 — `GET /` (and static assets) — **Backend owns serve; Frontend owns behavior**\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Method / path | `GET /` |\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Success | `200`, `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8`, body = SPA document that loads CSS/JS |\\n| Other methods on `/` | `405` `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"method_not_allowed\\\" }` **or** `404` JSON; must not `500` |\\n\\n**Also serve (same task):**\\n| Path | Type | Notes |\\n|------|------|-------|\\n| `GET /css/app.css` | `text/css; charset=utf-8` | From `public/css/app.css` |\\n| `GET /js/app.js`, `GET /js/auth.js` (and any other files under `public/js/`) | `application/javascript; charset=utf-8` | Path traversal forbidden |\\n| `GET /` only as HTML entry | — | Do **not** require `/index.html` for acceptance; optional redirect/`index.html` alias is allowed |\\n\\n**Routing order in `server/index.js` (must preserve API contracts):**\\n1. `GET /api/health` (unchanged)\\n2. Auth API via `handleAuthRoutes` (unchanged)\\n3. Static / SPA handler for safe paths under `public/`\\n4. Else `404` `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"not_found\\\" }`\\n\\n**Path safety:** resolve files under `path.join(__dirname, '..', 'public')` (or `/app/public`); reject `..` segments; never serve outside `public/`. Missing file → `404` JSON (same envelope as today) or plain 404 — not `500`.\\n\\n**Client while slow:** N/A for document fetch beyond browser load; if CSS/JS 404, auth UI may be unstyled but HTML structure with testids must still be present in the HTML (prefer embedding critical hooks in `index.html`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-2 — Client → `POST /api/auth/register` (consume MARATHON-3 C1)\\n\\n| Client sends | `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string, \\\"display_name\\\"?: string }` |\\n| Success | `201` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Errors | `400` / `409` / `5xx` with `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` when provided |\\n\\n**Client ownership:**\\n- Serialize JSON; **MUST NOT** require or gate on `email`.\\n- On submit: disable `auth-submit` (or equivalent pending state) until response settles.\\n- On `201`: `localStorage.setItem('huddle.token', token)`; set current user from `user`; hide `#auth-modal`; show authenticated chrome (**auto-login**).\\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string **visibly** inside the auth form (dedicated error element adjacent to the form; must be readable without opening DevTools).\\n- On network failure / `5xx`: show a visible generic message (e.g. “Something went wrong”); do not clear an existing valid token unless this was not a logged-in flow.\\n- Optional client pre-check (username regex / password length) may run before fetch; **server remains authoritative** — still handle server errors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-3 — Client → `POST /api/auth/login` (consume MARATHON-3 C2)\\n\\nSame as register for storage and error visibility; success status is `200`. Wrong password / unknown user → `401` → visible error; **MUST NOT** enter authenticated shell.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-4 — Client → `GET /api/auth/me` (consume MARATHON-3 C3)\\n\\n| When | App boot if `huddle.token` present; optionally after login |\\n| Header | `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Success `200` | Enter shell with `user`; keep token |\\n| `401` | `localStorage.removeItem('huddle.token')`; show `#auth-modal`; clear `current-user` |\\n| Network / `5xx` while booting with a token | Show auth modal **or** a non-claiming loading state, then fall back to auth modal; **MUST NOT** leave a forged `current-user` without a successful `/me` or prior successful register/login in this page life. Prefer: treat boot failure like logged-out after clear-or-keep policy — **decision: on boot network/`5xx`, keep token in storage but show a visible retry/error in the modal region and do not mark user logged-in; user can retry or clear via attempting login. On `401`, always clear token.** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-5 — Logout / re-login (client-only)\\n\\n| Action | Behavior |\\n|--------|----------|\\n| Click `logout-btn` | Remove `huddle.token`; clear in-memory `user` and any shell selection state this task owns; hide authenticated chrome; show `#auth-modal` in **login** mode; clear password fields |\\n| Login again (same or other user) | On `200`, store new token, show shell with new `user` |\\n| “Restores workspace” meaning for **this** task | Re-entering the authenticated shell after logout→login (and after hard reload with valid token). **Domain** workspace/channel/message tree reload is **MARATHON-22**: this task exposes a stable “session became authenticated” / “session cleared” seam (e.g. `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('huddle:auth', { detail: { user } }))` and `huddle:logout`) so 22 can refetch. Until 22 lands, shell may be empty — that is success for 21 |\\n\\n**MUST NOT:** call a non-existent logout API; leave `huddle.token` set after logout; show `current-user` while modal is the active unauthenticated UI.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C-SPA-6 — DOM contract (QA / Playwright)\\n\\nExact attributes (implementer must not rename):\\n\\n| Hook | Requirement |\\n|------|-------------|\\n| `#auth-modal` | Present in DOM; visible when logged out; not the primary interactive surface when logged in (hidden via CSS `display:none` / `hidden` attribute / equivalent) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"]` | The sign-up/login `\\u003cform\\u003e` inside the modal |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-submit\\\"]` | Submit control (button or input) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"auth-toggle\\\"]` | Control that switches between Sign up and Log in modes |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"current-user\\\"]` | Visible when authenticated; text identifies the user (`display_name`) |\\n| `[data-testid=\\\"logout-btn\\\"]` | Visible when authenticated; triggers C-SPA-5 |\\n\\nForm fields (recommended stable hooks for typing; if not testid-pinned by task, use `name` attributes):\\n- `name=\\\"username\\\"`, `name=\\\"password\\\"`\\n- Optional `name=\\\"display_name\\\"` visible **only** in sign-up mode\\n\\nError surface: an element inside `#auth-modal` / `auth-form` that displays the latest error string (e.g. `data-testid=\\\"auth-error\\\"` is **recommended** for clarity but **not** required by the task text — if omitted, error text must still be visible in the modal).\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Server schema\\n**No SQLite / API schema changes.** Reuses MARATHON-3 `users` / `tokens` and `UserObj`.\\n\\n### Browser persistence\\n| Key | Type | Nullability | Notes |\\n|-----|------|-------------|-------|\\n| `localStorage['huddle.token']` | string | absent when logged out | Opaque bearer ≥16 chars from API; never store password |\\n| In-memory `currentUser` | `UserObj` \\\\| null | null when logged out | Rebuilt from register/login/`/me`; not the durability source |\\n\\n### Backward compatibility\\nAdding `GET /` HTML where unknown paths previously returned JSON `404` is an intentional behavior change for `/` and static paths only. All `/api/*` contracts remain unchanged.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `public/index.html` | SPA shell: `#auth-modal`, form with pinned testids, `#app-shell`, links to CSS/JS |\\n| `public/css/app.css` | Layout for auth modal + minimal authenticated chrome; usable at 1280×900 |\\n| `public/js/auth.js` | Token get/set/clear; `register` / `login` / `me` fetch helpers; Bearer header helper |\\n| `public/js/app.js` | Boot, mode toggle, submit handlers, logout, show/hide modal vs shell, populate `current-user` |\\n| `server/static.js` | `handleStatic(req, res, pathname) → boolean`: map `/` → `index.html`, safe file serve under `public/`, correct Content-Types |\\n\\n### Modify\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/index.js` | After health + auth routes, call `handleStatic`; only then JSON 404. Do not alter health/auth status codes |\\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Optional: add `sendText(res, status, body, contentType)` used by static handler — keep `sendJson`/`readJson` behavior identical |\\n| `test/server.test.js` (optional but recommended) | Assert `GET /` returns `200` and `text/html` containing `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`; assert `/api/health` still JSON |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/db.js` | Auth API owned by MARATHON-3; no logout endpoint in this task |\\n| `start.sh`, `redis.conf` | Cluster bootstrap unchanged; static files need no extra process |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\\n| Workspace/channel/message UI | MARATHON-22 / 23 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Within this task\\n1. `public/index.html` + CSS skeleton with pinned hooks  \\n2. `server/static.js` + wire `index.js` so `GET /` works on any node  \\n3. `auth.js` API helpers  \\n4. `app.js` boot / submit / logout flows  \\n5. Manual check: register → token in localStorage → reload → still logged in → logout → login  \\n\\n### Parallelism\\n- Frontend implementer owns `public/**` + static routing.\\n- Backend auth already closed (MARATHON-3); do not block on MARATHON-4/5.\\n- MARATHON-22 **architecture/implementation** depends on: authenticated shell mount, `huddle.token`, `huddle:auth` / `huddle:logout` events (or equivalent documented callbacks), and existing testids remaining stable.\\n\\n### Seams this task owns\\n| Seam | Downstream |\\n|------|------------|\\n| `GET /` HTML + static assets | QA; all SPA tasks |\\n| `huddle.token` read/write/clear | MARATHON-22/23 fetch; MARATHON-18 WS `?token=` can read same key |\\n| DOM testids / `#auth-modal` | QA automation |\\n| Auth session events / `#app-shell` | MARATHON-22 three-pane; MARATHON-23 modals |\\n\\n### Build order\\n- **Requires:** MARATHON-3 endpoints on the integrated head (present).\\n- **Blocks:** Meaningful MARATHON-22 UI (declared dependent).\\n- **Does not block:** MARATHON-4/5 backend work.\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\\n| Cut | Owner |\\n|-----|--------|\\n| Workspaces, channels, three-pane, messages, their testids | MARATHON-22 |\\n| Threads, reactions, settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\\n| Profile PATCH UI | MARATHON-23 (API MARATHON-4) |\\n| Server token revoke / logout API | New task if ever required |\\n| Client-side router for deep links beyond `/` | MARATHON-22 if needed |\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\nNeighborhood scan (`server/`, `server/auth/`, `test/`, repo greps for `localStorage`, `auth-form`, `SPA`, `static`, `index.html`):\\n\\n| Finding | Why excluded |\\n|---------|----------------|\\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me | Already implemented (MARATHON-3); consume only |\\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` / tokens / users / passwords | No change |\\n| `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\\n| `test/auth.test.js` API contract tests | Remain backend-focused; optional SPA smoke is this task only if added under Files to Modify |\\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Workspaces / channels / messages UI + testids | MARATHON-22 |\\n| Threads / reactions / settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\\n| WS subscribe / `?token=` | MARATHON-18 |\\n| IRC gateway | MARATHON-20 |\\n| Server-side logout / token TTL | Explicitly deferred in MARATHON-3 |\\n| Email, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / unspecified |\\n\\nNo existing `public/` tree or `huddle.token` client code was found — greenfield SPA.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Empty username/password submit | Client may block with visible validation **or** send and show server `400`; either way user sees an error; no silent no-op |\\n| Password length \\u0026lt; 8 on register | Visible error (client and/or server `400`) |\\n| Duplicate username | Show server `409` `error` text in form |\\n| Invalid credentials on login | Show error; stay on modal; token unset |\\n| Double-click submit | Ignore second submit while request in flight (disable button) |\\n| `localStorage` unavailable / throws | Show visible error that auth cannot persist; do not pretend success |\\n| Stale token on boot (`401` from `/me`) | Clear `huddle.token`; show modal; no shell |\\n| Boot with token, network down | Do not show a fake user; show modal or retry UI; keep token until `401` or explicit logout |\\n| Logout | Token removed synchronously before UI switches; `current-user` cleared |\\n| Login as user B after user A | Shell shows B’s `display_name`; no leftover A identity in chrome |\\n| Hard reload while logged in | Token survives; `/me` restores shell |\\n| `GET /` on `:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002` | Identical SPA (any node) |\\n| Request `GET /../../etc/passwd` style path | Rejected; `404`; no file leak |\\n| `POST /` | Not an API; `405` or `404`; not `500` |\\n| Auth API still JSON | Static handler must not intercept `/api/*` |\\n| Toggle sign-up ↔ login | Clears or retains username per UX choice; **must** clear visible error; password field cleared on toggle **recommended** |\\n| Viewport 1280×900 | Auth modal and chrome fully usable; no reliance on hover-only controls for submit/logout/toggle |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and `:8001`, `:8002`) returns **200** HTML for the SPA (not JSON `not_found`).\\n2. HTML includes `#auth-modal` and elements with `data-testid` values **`auth-form`**, **`auth-submit`**, **`auth-toggle`**, **`current-user`**, **`logout-btn`**.\\n3. From a logged-out state, user can **sign up** with valid username/password; on success they are **immediately authenticated** (modal dismissed; `current-user` shows identity) without a separate manual login step.\\n4. After sign-up/login success, `localStorage.getItem('huddle.token')` is a non-empty string (length ≥ 16).\\n5. Invalid register (short password, bad username) shows a **visible** error in the auth UI; user remains logged out; token **MUST NOT** be set.\\n6. Login with wrong password shows a **visible** error; token **MUST NOT** be set; shell **MUST NOT** appear.\\n7. `auth-toggle` switches the form between sign-up and login modes without full page navigation.\\n8. Clicking `logout-btn` clears `huddle.token`, hides authenticated chrome, and shows `#auth-modal` again.\\n9. After logout, logging in again returns the user to the authenticated shell (session restored for SPA purposes).\\n10. Hard reload with a valid token still logged-in (via `/api/auth/me`); hard reload after logout stays logged-out.\\n11. Layout is operable at **1280×900**.\\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or `/api/auth/*` response shapes/status codes.\\n13. **MUST NOT** require `email` in the form as a mandatory field.\\n14. **MUST NOT** introduce remote CDNs, Slack SDK, or a frontend build that `start.sh` must run.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (implementer)\\n- Unit/integration: `GET /` → 200 + `text/html` + substring `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`.\\n- Existing `test/auth.test.js` still passes (API unchanged).\\n- Optional: static path traversal attempt returns 404.\\n\\n### Manual / browser (human or QA)\\n1. Start cluster (`./start.sh`); open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\\n2. Sign up `alice` / `password1` → see `current-user`, DevTools Application → `huddle.token` set.\\n3. Reload → still logged in.\\n4. Logout → token gone, modal visible.\\n5. Login → shell returns.\\n6. Toggle to sign-up, try password `short` → visible error.\\n7. Repeat smoke on `:8001` (register on 8000, open 8001 with same origin storage is per-port — use login on 8001 with same credentials to prove API; note **localStorage is origin-scoped per port**, so cross-port auto-session is **not** required; cross-node token validity remains a backend property).\\n\\n### Explicit non-goals for verification\\nWorkspace lists, messages, threads, WS — verify only auth shell + token lifecycle here.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"SPA shell served from GET / on any node via public/ + server/static.js. Auth uses huddle.token, pinned testids, client-only logout, huddle:auth/huddle:logout events + #app-shell for MARATHON-22. Verified unit tests + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/logout/reload/validation).\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.142443715Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:58:35.262638318Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up/login form with visible validation errors; auto-login on success; logout/login restores workspace. Store token in localStorage huddle.token. Pin data-testid: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, current-user, logout-btn; ids auth-modal. Drivable at 1280x900.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-22\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: workspaces, channels, three-pane layout, messages\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.163337652Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 25,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"author\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=628888f2468a11570f68c14732c72e1d8893260d\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:58:35.238705649Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nloom-prompts\npackage.json\nredis.conf\nserver\nstart.sh\ntest\ntimer.sh\n","localExecutionTimeMs":48},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch MARATHON-21 task design via loom"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-4f7f68fb-377f-46bf-ba96-2649525f7485-18\nfc_e42ee057-0fe4-9981-9411-fea635b204e3_0","startedAtMs":"1787428777430","completedAtMs":"1787428777529"},"model_call_id":"aea25036-a8b1-4c82-8550-6752316bd60c-4-mnaw","session_id":"8c969c8e-77c9-4261-a386-a66451852833","timestamp_ms":1787428777574}
